------------------------------------------------------------------
Baseline: stuff 1091ee26d04ea2b38b090ec988a4a54c6ca4ebfa.
Same upstream, OpenSCAD and BOSL2 pins as above. The Printables flattened
single-file copy is a reading aid only; all citations use the vendored files.

Additional plate renders use the one-tile command above with these -D values:
  openconnect_nubs_right.stl: slot_lock_side="Right"
  openconnect_nubs_both.stl: slot_lock_side="Both"
  openconnect_nubs_none.stl: slot_lock_distribution="None"
  openconnect_flip.stl: slot_entryramp_flip=true
  openconnect_edge_top.stl: slot_edge_feature_widen="Top"
  openconnect_edge_side.stl: slot_edge_feature_widen="Side"
  openconnect_edge_none.stl: slot_edge_feature_widen="None"

The additional mesh/*.scad files are this repo's wrappers, not upstream.
Render slide_down, slide_left, slide_right, excess_thickness and excess_length:
  OPENSCADPATH=$BOSL2_PARENT openscad --export-format=binstl \
    -o mesh/openconnect_<variant>.stl mesh/openconnect_<variant>.scad

The grid spin values at openconnect_lib.scad:467 are passed to a BOTTOM
attachment (:484); they are not direct world-Z rotations. Author left/right
meshes match world-Z +90/-90 respectively. Direct -90/+90 rotation differs
by 9.1638 mm; reversing the spin gives <=0.003536 mm surface distance.

